{"seq":353,"at":"2026-08-25T19:05:58Z","event":"answer","id":"Q322","state":"chosen","option":"c","note":"Owner correction (chat): an untouched bucket ADDS 0, it does not multiply by 0. Worked example, verbatim: \"row + col + diag = 0 + 0 + 0. Row gets 10 score. it is now 10 + 0 + 0 = 10. Col gets 5 score. It is now 10 * 5 + 0 = 50. Diag gets 2 score. It is now 10 * 5 * 2 = 100.\" So grid score = the PRODUCT of every bucket that has scored, and 0 when none has. This is arithmetically what (c) already said, restated in the owner's own terms, which are clearer.","override":true,"round":3}
{"seq":354,"at":"2026-08-25T19:05:58Z","event":"answer","id":"Q326","state":"chosen","option":null,"note":"Owner correction (chat), superseding the round-2 answer (b): \"do not display subtotals such as grid score.\" No per-grid score, no per-grid bucket breakdown. The HUD shows the board total and the combo, and nothing else. This also settles the Q123/Q326 conflict in favour of Q123, which said no per-grid subtotal all along.","override":true,"round":3}
{"seq":355,"at":"2026-08-25T19:05:58Z","event":"answer","id":"Q233","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Owner refinement (chat): \"rng is going to need its own in depth generator, so seed generation is its own todo for later, we just have placeholder seed generation for now.\" The seeded-from-state contract stands; the SEED DERIVATION ships as an explicit placeholder with a todo.md item, and no shipped card may depend on foreseeing a future slot until the real generator lands.","override":true,"round":3}
{"seq":356,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q34","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Owner reversal (chat): randomised refill ABANDONED. Verbatim: \"lets just abandon the randomized refill for now then since I realize it doesnt make sense with current way effect processing works from left to right. Use current system where leftmost draws first, then next on right since it is next card triggering draw effect.\" So the refill is strictly left-to-right, driven by each entrance header card in board order, exactly as TypeInput.draw_card does today. This resolves the Q34/Q207 conflict I raised: no coordinator is needed because there is nothing to coordinate.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":357,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q35","state":"chosen","option":null,"note":"Moot: Q34 abandoned randomised slot assignment, so there are no random slots to spread.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":358,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q233","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Scope narrowed by the Q34 reversal: the refill no longer uses RNG at all, so the determinism ruling is satisfied by construction rather than by seeding. The deck SHUFFLE at game start keeps its existing RNG, unchanged. The in-depth generator remains a todo.md item, no longer coupled to the Entrance.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":359,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q205","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Owner refinement (chat): \"sure measure it as we implement and note how much it hurts performance wise during tests.\" So the measurement is not deferred to when it hurts — it is taken during implementation and the numbers are recorded in the test output, against the existing scoring_cost harness.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":360,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q133","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Owner refinement (chat): \"the goal curve refit can be its own phase if you think its too big to be 1 step.\" It is. The refit becomes its own numbered phase in PLAN.md with its own acceptance gate, not a step inside another phase.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":361,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:18Z","event":"answer","id":"Q322","state":"chosen","option":"c","note":"Owner confirmation (chat) of the edge I assumed: \"assumption is correct. if score is 0 do not multiply regardless of if 0 is somehow a returned actual score from something.\" So the test is the VALUE, never touched-ness: a bucket worth 0 is excluded from the product even when a line genuinely completed and scored 0.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":362,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:30Z","event":"answer","id":"Q160","state":"chosen","option":null,"note":"Owner specification (chat), superseding the earlier prose: \"one scroll container inside the picture to deal with tall stacks and potentially infinite grids or very large grids. Camera will pan over 3 possible grid positions since that is size of picture frame, and user can then choose to further scroll to reveal more of a single grid. choosing to pan left and right will shift current view of 3 grids left or right if there are more than 3 grids off edge of picture frame.\" So the two mechanisms divide cleanly: the WALL CAMERA steps between the 3 grid positions the picture frame holds, and ONE scroll container inside the picture handles tall stacks and any reveal beyond those three.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":363,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:30Z","event":"answer","id":"Q145","state":"chosen","option":"a","note":"Owner addition (chat): the show OPENS zoomed out. \"game starts zoomed out, then you choose a grid which zooms in, then you can go left and right.\" That opening state was not previously recorded anywhere.","override":true,"round":4}
{"seq":364,"at":"2026-08-26T11:35:30Z","event":"answer","id":"Q154","state":"chosen","option":"b","note":"Owner resolution (chat) of the conflict I raised with Q14=(b) no panels: no dedicated position indicator is needed because the NAVIGATION carries the information — you start zoomed out, choose a grid, and pan from there. Verbatim: \"I will probably make it more obvious down the line by having background art be unique by location.\" Unique per-grid background art is a later content pass, not part of this design.","override":true,"round":4}
